<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     12. FEATURES IMPLEMENTED
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<h2><span class="section-num">12</span>Features Implemented</h2>

<h3>LangGraph Orchestration Engine</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Typed state machine with <code>StateGraph</code>, <code>Annotation.Root</code>, conditional edges, and <code>END</code>/<code>START</code> sentinels</li>
  <li>Two-node pipeline: <code>planner</code> (LLM planning) → <code>runStep</code> (loop)</li>
  <li>Conditional routing based on runtime state (<code>phase</code>, <code>plan.length</code>, <code>aborted</code>)</li>
  <li>Recursion-limited execution with <code>AbortSignal</code> support for cancellation</li>
  <li>Agent handoff notes using structured delimiters (<code>[HANDOFF_START]…[HANDOFF_END]</code>)</li>
  <li>5-minute per-step idle timeout; 2-minute handoff timeout</li>
  <li>Live plan persistence to PostgreSQL after each state transition</li>
  <li>Full message log (<code>AgentMessage</code>) for every event: task dispatch, agent response, handoff, error, completion</li>
</ul>

<h3>Agent &amp; Machine Registry</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Register remote machines with SSH credentials (stored AES-256 encrypted)</li>
  <li>Register AI agents (Claude Code, Aider, custom) with configurable idle markers</li>
  <li>Machine health / connectivity status tracking</li>
</ul>

<h3>Session Management</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Create sessions with a goal, supervisor model selection, and agent roster</li>
  <li>Start / stop / view sessions</li>
  <li>Real-time plan view (step index, status per step, handoff notes)</li>
</ul>

<h3>Terminal Infrastructure</h3>
<ul>
  <li>SSH connection management per machine</li>
  <li>tmux session lifecycle per agent (<code>new-session</code>, <code>send-keys</code>, <code>capture-pane</code>)</li>
  <li>Idle detection by polling for the agent's configured prompt marker</li>
  <li>Handoff note extraction by regex over captured terminal output</li>
</ul>

<h3>Knowledge Editor (broader product context)</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Block-based editing with Tiptap (callout, toggle, wikilink, slash commands)</li>
  <li>Canonical AST storage in PostgreSQL (<code>Note</code> + <code>Block</code> tables)</li>
  <li>Wikilinks, backlinks, graph projection, tag extraction</li>
  <li>Markdown &amp; MDX export, public note routes, folder hierarchy</li>
  <li>Docker Compose production stack with multi-arch image publishing via GitHub Actions</li>
</ul>


<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     13. SETUP & RUNNING
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<h2><span class="section-num">13</span>Setup &amp; Running the Project</h2>

<h3>Prerequisites</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Node.js 20+</li>
  <li>Docker &amp; Docker Compose</li>
  <li>An OpenAI API key (for the orchestrator's planner LLM)</li>
  <li>At least one remote machine with SSH access and a supported AI CLI tool installed</li>
</ul>

<h3>Step-by-Step Local Setup</h3>

<pre># 1. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/GiraffeGraph/giraffle.git
cd giraffle

# 2. Install dependencies
npm install

# 3. Start PostgreSQL
docker compose up -d

# 4. Configure environment
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env — required values:
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/giraffle
#   AUTH_SECRET=&lt;random-64-char-string&gt;
#   NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
#   OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# 5. Run database migrations
npx prisma migrate dev

# 6. Start the development server
npm run dev</pre>

<p>Open <code>http://localhost:3000</code>. Register an account, then navigate to <strong>/agents</strong> to register machines and agents.</p>

<h3>Running the Verification Suite</h3>

<pre># Type-check, lint, unit tests, and production build
npm run verify

# Unit tests only
npm run test:run

# Coverage report
npm run test:coverage</pre>

<h3>Production Deployment (Docker)</h3>

<pre>cp .env.production.example .env.production
# Edit .env.production
./scripts/prod-up.sh</pre>

<h3>Step-by-Step: Using the LangGraph Orchestrator</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Go to <strong>/agents</strong> → "Machines" tab → Add a machine (host, SSH credentials).</li>
  <li>Go to "Agents" tab → Add an agent (link to a machine, set the agent command and idle marker).</li>
  <li>Go to "Sessions" tab → Create a new session (enter a goal, choose agents, pick supervisor model).</li>
  <li>Click <strong>Start</strong>. The LangGraph state machine invokes the planner (calls GPT-4o), produces a plan, then executes each step sequentially.</li>
  <li>Watch live progress in the session detail page — each step shows its status and the handoff note passed to the next agent.</li>
</ol>


